      <memberdef kind="function" id="classbioscara__hardware__interfaces_1_1BioscaraGripperHardwareInterface_1a44d87744318928ac5ba54096764a3bcc" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>hardware_interface::CallbackReturn</type>
        <definition>hardware_interface::CallbackReturn bioscara_hardware_interfaces::BioscaraGripperHardwareInterface::on_error</definition>
        <argsstring>(const rclcpp_lifecycle::State &amp;previous_state) override</argsstring>
        <name>on_error</name>
        <qualifiedname>bioscara_hardware_interfaces::BioscaraGripperHardwareInterface::on_error</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const rclcpp_lifecycle::State &amp;</type>
          <declname>previous_state</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Called when an error in any state or state transition is thrown. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>According to the <ulink url="https://control.ros.org/jazzy/doc/ros2_control/hardware_interface/doc/hardware_components_userdoc.html#handling-of-errors-that-happen-during-read-and-write-calls">ros2_control documentation</ulink>:</para>
<para><blockquote><para><zwj/>Error handling follows the node lifecycle. If successful CallbackReturn::SUCCESS is returned and hardware is again in <computeroutput>UNCONFIGURED</computeroutput> state, if any ERROR or FAILURE happens the hardware ends in <computeroutput>FINALIZED</computeroutput> state and can not be recovered. The only option is to reload the complete plugin, but there is currently no service for this in the Controller Manager. </para>
</blockquote></para>
<para>Since the hardware will immediatly return to the <computeroutput>unconfigured</computeroutput> state (<ulink url="https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/blob/d0836b7f12b89acb89bde83d4ba4308513b03204/hardware_interface/src/hardware_component.cpp#L247">source</ulink>) if the error could be handled we manually call the transition functions which would normally be called to this state. Those are:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Previous state</bold>: <computeroutput>active</computeroutput><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Deactivate hardware (<ref refid="classbioscara__hardware__interfaces_1_1BioscaraGripperHardwareInterface_1ab199edb3ee4a278fc8f5a24c2536fc14" kindref="member">on_deactivate()</ref>) -&gt; <computeroutput>inactive</computeroutput></para>
